      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To handle the situation, immediately isolate the affected container from the rest of the shipment to prevent further temperature escalation. Assess the current temperature and time-temperature control history to determine the extent of the temperature excursion. Then, suspend loading/unloading operations and contact the carrier to report the failure and request rerouting or rephasing of the shipment to a nearby depot to shore up inventory and possibly redistribute the goods. \n Protocol for safe handling and sale of the batch must be determined by a qualified food safety professional who conducts a temperature-log review, to assess the possible bacterial growth and thus arrive at a successful conclusion.",
